  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12-2000-p7.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(\\log_b 729 = n,\\) then \\(b^n = 729 = 3^6,\\) so \\(n\\) must be a positive divisor of \\(6.\\)\n\nThe possibilities \\(n = 1, 2, 3, 6\\) give \\(b = 3^6, 3^3, 3^2, 3^1,\\) that is, \\(729, 27, 9,\\) and \\(3.\\)\n\nThere are \\(4\\) such values of \\(b.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "If \\(\\log_b 729 = n,\\) then \\(b^n = 729 = 3^6\\)",
        "For \\(b\\) to be an integer, \\(n\\) must be a positive divisor of \\(6\\)"
      ],
